ld black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]suggestions, `task_block_id`)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]bob-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-contract: extend `bob capture-complete` with the `task_block_id` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]context, the additive `block_id` object (intent, marker range, body, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]allowed-character rule, used IDs, suggestions), link-only candidates [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with Pomodoro annotations, and the project-note `+` replacement fix; [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update docs and tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mac: generalize the Active Task Picker into a source-agnostic [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]capture picker[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]picker-generalize[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]picker-generalize: refactor the `^` picker's presentation types, model [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state machine, routing, controller focus repair, filter field, and card [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]into source-agnostic `CapturePicker*` building blocks with zero [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]user-visible change to `^`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mac CaptureCore: decode the block-ID contract and build the [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]Block ID Picker engine[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]block-id-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bob-contract, picker-generalize[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]block-id-core: decode the `block_id` object and `task_block_id` context,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add Bob-driven ID rules, and build the link and new-ID presentation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine on the generic picker types, with real-bob fixtures and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exhaustive tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mac app: Block ID 